{
  "schema": "job-v1",
  "job": "litectx-maintainer",
  "description": "litectx-maintainer \u2014 authored through the bareloop interview (hitl, js) against /home/hamr/PycharmProjects/bareloop-patients/litectx-maintainer",
  "provider": "anthropic-api",
  "cadence": {
    "unit": "day",
    "every": 1
  },
  "budgetUsd": 5,
  "maxWallMs": 4500000,
  "writeScope": [
    "src/"
  ],
  "goal": "Get src/ to zero errors under npx tsc --strict --noEmit, with no @ts-ignore/@ts-expect-error/@ts-nocheck and no new any, npm test still exiting 0, and nothing outside src/ changed.",
  "escalation": {
    "mode": "decision-ready"
  },
  "verdictType": "hitl",
  "closeDecl": {
    "genre": "TYPES",
    "lang": "js",
    "stages": [
      {
        "name": "changed-from-seed",
        "kind": "files-changed",
        "params": {
          "requireNonEmpty": true,
          "allowPrefixes": [
            "src/"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "typecheck-src-errors",
        "kind": "count-not-worse",
        "params": {
          "cmd": "npx",
          "args": [
            "tsc",
            "--strict",
            "--noEmit"
          ],
          "parser": {
            "terms": [
              {
                "lineMatch": "error TS\\d+",
                "capture": null,
                "sign": 1,
                "aggregate": "sum",
                "region": "whole-output"
              }
            ]
          },
          "scope": {
            "includePrefixes": [
              "src/"
            ]
          },
          "direction": "lower-is-better",
          "baseline": 0
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "typecheck-outside-errors",
        "kind": "count-not-worse",
        "params": {
          "cmd": "npx",
          "args": [
            "tsc",
            "--strict",
            "--noEmit"
          ],
          "parser": {
            "terms": [
              {
                "lineMatch": "error TS\\d+",
                "capture": null,
                "sign": 1,
                "aggregate": "sum",
                "region": "whole-output"
              }
            ]
          },
          "scope": {
            "excludePrefixes": [
              "src/"
            ]
          },
          "direction": "lower-is-better",
          "baseline": "seed"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "tests-kept",
        "kind": "count-not-worse",
        "params": {
          "cmd": "node",
          "args": [
            "--test"
          ],
          "parser": {
            "terms": [
              {
                "lineMatch": "^# tests (\\d+)$",
                "capture": 1,
                "sign": 1,
                "aggregate": "first",
                "region": "whole-output"
              }
            ]
          },
          "scope": {
            "includePrefixes": [
              "test/"
            ]
          },
          "direction": "higher-is-better",
          "baseline": "seed"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "suite-green-exit",
        "kind": "command-exit",
        "params": {
          "cmd": "node",
          "args": [
            "--test"
          ],
          "expectExit": 0
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "suite-green-zero-failures",
        "kind": "count-not-worse",
        "params": {
          "cmd": "node",
          "args": [
            "--test"
          ],
          "parser": {
            "terms": [
              {
                "lineMatch": "^# fail (\\d+)$",
                "capture": 1,
                "sign": 1,
                "aggregate": "first",
                "region": "whole-output"
              }
            ]
          },
          "scope": {
            "includePrefixes": [
              "test/"
            ]
          },
          "direction": "lower-is-better",
          "baseline": 0
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "no-suppressions",
        "kind": "pattern-absent-in-diff",
        "params": {
          "patterns": [
            {
              "id": "ts-ignore",
              "regex": "@ts-ignore"
            },
            {
              "id": "ts-expect-error",
              "regex": "@ts-expect-error"
            },
            {
              "id": "ts-nocheck",
              "regex": "@ts-nocheck"
            },
            {
              "id": "eslint-disable",
              "regex": "eslint-disable"
            },
            {
              "id": "any",
              "regex": "(?:[{<|(\\[:,]|\\bas)\\s*any\\b|\\bany\\[\\]"
            },
            {
              "id": "any-star",
              "regex": "@\\w+\\s*\\{\\s*[*?]\\s*\\}"
            },
            {
              "id": "cast",
              "regex": "@type\\s*\\{.*\\}\\s*\\*\\/\\s*\\("
            }
          ],
          "extensions": [
            ".js",
            ".mjs",
            ".cjs"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "human-confirms-real-fixes",
        "kind": "human-confirms",
        "params": {
          "ask": "Look at the diff in src/: are the type errors genuinely fixed (real type annotations/logic corrections), with nothing silenced, ts-ignored, or cast away just to make the checker pass?"
        }
      }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Re-submitted unchanged after seed-read review: the seed signature is as expected for unstarted work \u2014 changed-from-seed red (no work done yet), typecheck-src-errors red at 64 (real baseline-0 errors in src/), typecheck-outside-errors green (0 errors outside src/, baseline measured in place), tests-kept and suite-green stages green (423 tests executed at seed, 0 failures, baseline measured in place), no-suppressions green (no diff yet). This confirms the instruments are measuring the right populations and will correctly grade the real work once src/ is fixed.",
      "src/**/*.js matched no files in the seed listing even though src/assemble.js and src/chunker.js appear in the measured tsc output \u2014 the seed file listing under sourcePaths was apparently stale/incomplete for src/*.js; allowPrefixes and scope for src/ are used as given in the interview and facts since src/ is the named target directory.",
      "No path-bearing fact was available for the exact list of src/*.js files, so scope includePrefixes for src/ stages is left as the directory prefix 'src/' rather than enumerated files.",
      "human-confirms stage correctly shows 'skipped' at seed since it only renders after the mechanical stages pass; this is expected and not an error."
    ]
  }
}
